    {
      "id": "0sh9w7z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.5 Olive Ridley Sea Turtles"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3ktpgmg",
      "content": "Odisha's coast is the world's most important nesting ground for Olive Ridley sea turtles (Lepidochelys olivacea). Mass nesting (Arribada) occurs at three main sites:"
    },
    {
      "id": "puuvsmc",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Gahirmatha Beach (Kendrapara) – World's largest Olive Ridley rookery; protected by Gahirmatha Marine Sanctuary",
        "Rushikulya River Mouth (Ganjam) – Second most important site",
        "Devi River Mouth (Puri district) – Third important nesting site"
      ]
    }
  ],
